# RESOLVED 2026-08-09: 8422ece8 (#1638) restored, and _merge_arrays_cache_entries
# DELETED as stale. It had zero references anywhere in the tree, upstream does not
# define it at all, and our copy is byte-identical to upstream's last pre-deletion
# version — so the fork never touched it: STALE, not FORK, by the conclusive test in
# AGENTS.md. Its only caller went away with 8422ece8's refactor. Same shape as
# models/cache.py::SlidingWindowCache.
#
# The rest of that commit is now in: dispatch.py's ~113-line inline APC lookup block
# became an 8-line `_apc.apc_lookup_plan(...)` call, `apc_extra_hash` now goes
# through `semantic_extra_hash` (see below), and ar.py's `_apc_prompt_cache_for_store`
# delegates to `snapshot_prompt_cache_row`.
#
# Two real bugs came out of it, neither with a failing test:
#   * The APC cache key was `tenant_scoped_hash(tenant, image_hash)` — audio, video,
#     inputs_embeds and masks were NOT in the key, so two requests differing only in
#     audio would share a prefix cache and reuse KV computed for other media.
#   * `_apc_prompt_cache_for_store` returned the LIVE prompt cache for single-row
#     batches instead of a clone, so a stored "checkpoint at N tokens" kept growing
#     as generation continued; it also never dequantized quantized layers.

