# --- mlx_vlm/utils.py
# RESOLVED 2026-08-10. `normalize_audio_features` was the last entry here and it is now
# DELETED, along with the whole region around it, so there is nothing left to excuse.
#
# The history is the useful part, because the entry was wrong twice before it was right.
# It began as a one-liner -- "stale half of dropped b93707d8; upstream folded it into
# the sanitize path" -- which was right about the classification and wrong about the
# scope: b93707d8 (#1498, "Always sanitize loaded weights and simplify audio
# preprocessing") did TWO independent things to utils.py and this tree had reverted both.
#
#   (a) load_model's sanitize block. #1498 deleted the `hasattr(model, "thinker")`
#       special case and added three `if hasattr(model_config, "<x>_config")` guards,
#       having moved the six-way thinker chain into qwen3_omni_moe.Model.sanitize. That
#       model-side half landed BYTE-IDENTICAL, so our copy both double-sanitized omni
#       AND reached `model_config.text_config` unguarded. FIXED in c5454e71: it was a
#       hard AttributeError on every `load_model` of minimax_m3, a real top-level
#       model_type (TEXT_ONLY in prompt_utils, its own tool parser) whose ModelConfig
#       has no `text_config`. The model could not be loaded at all.
#
#   (b) prepare_inputs' audio block. #1498 deleted the qwen3-omni special case
#       (`is_qwen3_omni_moe`, `audio_inputs`, `audio_feature_lengths`, `is_lossy_audio`
#       and this symbol) in favour of letting the processor do the feature extraction:
#       `process_inputs_with_fallback(..., audio=<arrays>)` returns `input_features` /
#       `feature_attention_mask`, the generic copy loop forwards them, and
#       qwen3_omni_moe/thinker.py:55 derives `audio_feature_lengths` when it is None.
#       Our copy was #1498's deleted text verbatim apart from one `print` -> `logger`.
#       DELETED 2026-08-10, on an explicit decision, after being deliberately held open
#       for one session: nothing in tests/ passed `audio=` to prepare_inputs, so a
#       ~60-line behaviour change on a path with zero coverage could not be validated.
#       The missing coverage is now written --
#       test_dropped_upstream_guards.py::TestOmniAudioFeaturesComeFromTheProcessor
#       asserts the contract the simplified path depends on (the processor receives
#       ARRAYS, and whatever it returns is forwarded) plus a tripwire against the branch
#       reappearing, which matters because a future merge re-offering pre-#1498 content
#       would produce no conflict -- the deleting commit is already an ancestor of main.
#
# Two things to carry forward. First: **a "stale half" entry should name the WHOLE
# region and say which sub-parts are resolved.** A per-symbol entry makes a two-region
# revert look like a one-symbol one, and this one hid a load-time crash for as long as
# it existed. Second: **holding an item open with the evidence written down is a valid
# outcome, and better than either guessing.** Marking it `# Fork:` would have laundered
# stale code into a documented feature; deleting it blind would have been an
# unvalidated behaviour change. Writing down exactly what was known, and what could not
# be known locally, is what made the decision a one-line answer later.
